{"findings": [
  {
    "id": "f01",
    "criterion": "Quantify project outcomes with specific metrics and data rather than vague descriptions.",
    "detail": "The portfolio opens and closes each project with numbers — 9/9 red-team attacks, 77.1% accuracy, 6.1× fewer tokens, 10,250 predictions, +$360/wk — so it follows this rule.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "dQ6RNltrXro",
        "start_seconds": 320.3,
        "quote": "quantify your contributions by using metrics and data to Showcase your impact"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f02",
    "criterion": "Include your location in the header/contact area so recruiters can immediately see where you are based.",
    "detail": "The visible header and footer contain name, role, GitHub and LinkedIn, but no city/region is shown.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk",
        "start_seconds": 522.8,
        "quote": "another big thing that is lacking here is his location this is one of the most important things a recruiter is going to look for in your application"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f03",
    "criterion": "Keep the header minimal: name, role, LinkedIn, GitHub, location; avoid photos, graphics, decorations and taglines.",
    "detail": "The page's hero contains the tagline 'I build agents and prove they work.' plus a stylized title '// applied-ai · measured', which is decorative/tagline-style content.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "3pFRqPqzBCM",
        "start_seconds": 115.2,
        "quote": "Add LinkedIn, GitHub, location, no photo, no graphics, no tagline."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f04",
    "criterion": "List concrete technologies/tools and show how you apply them, not just broad subject-area keywords.",
    "detail": "The page names 'agentic systems', 'RAG pipelines' and 'eval harnesses' as areas of work, but it does not present a skills section with specific languages/libraries such as Python, NumPy, Flask/FastAPI that demonstrate daily use.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "ZqqzBCg6IGU",
        "start_seconds": 140.6,
        "quote": "don't write things like machine learning or statistics under skills that is knowledge not a skill. Write how you apply that knowledge."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f05",
    "criterion": "For every serious project, provide a product-style explanation — problem, tech, challenges, learnings — and link to a fuller report/blog post.",
    "detail": "Each selected system is reduced to a one-line description and metric; the 'Case study →' labels are visible as text, but the homepage itself does not display the problem, challenges, or lessons learned for each project.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "ZqqzBCg6IGU",
        "start_seconds": 70.1,
        "quote": "Every project should have a one-page report or drive PDF link in your resume which should have what problem did you solve in this project, what text you used, what challenges did you face and what did you learn from those challenges."
      },
      {
        "video_id": "FpW8aiJPvts",
        "start_seconds": 333.7,
        "quote": "writing an accompanying blog post to the project just makes understanding your experience and skills much easier"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f06",
    "criterion": "Use metrics that are immediately intuitive to a non-technical recruiter, or explain unfamiliar technical measures.",
    "detail": "The page uses '0.93 answer parity', 'eval-verified accuracy', and '84.5% best answer F1' without defining these terms, which is the kind of metric that may not be intuitive to a recruiter.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "FpW8aiJPvts",
        "start_seconds": 333.7,
        "quote": "many metrics are also more intuitive for the recruiter a success rate of 95% is very intuitive an F1 score of 39 is perhaps not that intuitive if he doesn't know what that is but you get the point"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f07",
    "criterion": "Keep the whole document razor-focused on the specific job title/role you are targeting and avoid diluting it with unrelated areas.",
    "detail": "The page names 'Applied AI Engineer' as the role and every listed system is an AI/agent/RAG or data project, so it is tightly focused rather than diluted with unrelated work.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "by8wrrXW3So",
        "start_seconds": 1047.5,
        "quote": "You need to be razor focused on the job title that you want."
      },
      {
        "video_id": "fD0E57QYSPk",
        "start_seconds": 1061.5,
        "quote": "not specializing in too many different things it'll sort of water your application down"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "f08",
    "criterion": "Provide links to LinkedIn and a personal portfolio/GitHub so recruiters can easily learn more about you.",
    "detail": "The page is itself a personal GitHub Pages portfolio and the navigation/footer include GitHub and LinkedIn links, which matches this advice.",
    "contested": false,
    "citations": [
      {
        "video_id": "FpW8aiJPvts",
        "start_seconds": 333.7,
        "quote": "provide and embed links to Linkin ideally even a personal website blog posts and more"
      }
    ]
  }
]}
